Subject: [PATCH 35/35] Crime: off at server start; /crime on and /crime off
 switch it

Renn's CONCORD and crime rules start switched on.  They now start off
(<crime><Enabled>false</Enabled> and the code default), so new things
can be tested anywhere without CONCORD or flags.

/crime on turns them on while the server runs: systems already loaded
get their gate and station sentry guns.  /crime off clears every pilot's
flags (the clients are told), sends any CONCORD or police response away
and removes the sentry guns.  /crime with no arguments says which it is.
With crime off, taking from another pilot's can or wreck no longer
brings up the client's theft warning.

The kill rights migration is renamed from 20261011120000 to
20261013170000 so it runs after the incursion migrations on a database
that already has them.
